  (text "for small sensor board corner" (at 168.91 142.24 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 007b3cc8-f6d6-4ad8-9598-1d3139d411a3)
  )
  (text "mixed M2 and M2.5 to help guide orientation" (at 19.05 143.51 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 098a8304-7c94-4c49-862b-3439ac39f44d)
  )
  (text "leaving open the possibility of connecting a 5V (6V open circuit) solar panel directly\nzero ohm resistor is a failsafe for massive surges, placeholder for something else if needed"
    (at 173.99 121.92 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 0c1c987a-0792-4478-a15c-943eae2e31c7)
  )
  (text "TX = GP12\nRX = GP13\n\nSCL = GP19\nSDA = GP18" (at 166.37 53.34 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 2a17cc13-0107-4a06-a939-fc7c2c160e8e)
  )
  (text "use reduced vibration mountings" (at 204.47 149.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 2bb5db42-5763-41cf-abdf-b366cd446bbd)
  )
  (text "TVS" (at 254 161.29 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 9415834a-d3f1-4fd2-a252-50c207fd703d)
  )
  (text "Part of a Pi Pico" (at 162.56 41.91 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 9ce9cad8-8353-4bf2-8ee4-19bcccfb746b)
  )
  (text "basically, audio in more than 2 channels is a pain\nbut, this should offer 2x stereo pdm, 2x stereo i2s, or 1x tdm (some minor resistor changes required for anything other than i2s)\nPDM is more common now but usually only has interfaces for 1 or 2 mics, and is often lower bits/freq\ni2s is the most common, hence the primary output\nTDM is probably \"best\" for quad channel but is again, not as widely supported.\n\nThis should work with ESP32 with 2 i2s (S3, P4) or TDM (S3... C3)\nThis should work with Raspberry Pi Picos via PIO interfaces (examples can be found)\nThis may work with Nordic, but with one set of microphones to their PDM interface and one set to I2S, latency may differ\nTeensy 4.x via 2x i2s or TDM\nUse a microcontroller to USB audio for SBCs. Teensy probably easiest for that but Pico getting better.\n\n2x mic -> 1x pdm -> various\n4x mic -> 2x pdm -> pico pio, probably zephyr nordic, some stm\n4x mic -> 2x pdm -> adau7118 -> tdm -> some (teensy, esp certainly), probably pio\n4x mic -> 2x pdm -> 2x adau7112 -> 2x i2s -> various\n4x analog -> pcm1840 -> tdm (tried, bug on board)\n4x analog -> 2x stereo adc -> 2x i2s"
    (at 13.97 194.31 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid cd7f2dd7-771a-432f-a96c-e83446ae3e49)
  )
  (text "addr: 1101010b\nothers available with same package" (at 105.41 111.76 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid d0f110f5-9418-42c8-9857-c471b05a780e)
  )
  (text "resistive heating wire for\nsolar charging in cold\nmight also use a heat pack as a \"heat capacitor\""
    (at 127 196.85 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid d4e1b809-2dfc-4084-90fa-9bf5e13f49e7)
  )
  (text "on pico, prevent flow in downstream pin" (at 107.95 33.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid dc18b506-bd7b-4d01-8fa3-f524d566188d)
  )
  (text "Keep currents higher than 10 mA a few millimeters away from the sensor IC\nheading = atan2(y, x) * 180 / PI + declination  (adjust from accelerometer)\nthis can't take 1.8V as input power"
    (at 195.58 33.02 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid e9d40138-914e-4b4e-ac92-3aaeeb7d33e3)
  )

